index 8674a53..54de62f 100644
--- a/docs/intent/previews/previews-design.md
+++ b/docs/intent/previews/previews-design.md
@@ -23,4 +23,12 @@ Resolve the immutable source revision before rendering. The cache key includes c
 
 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The cache uses a **2Q eviction policy** with two FIFO queues: **Am** (first-use entries) and **A1** (reused entries). On a cache miss, a new entry is inserted at the head of Am with a size accounting for its JPEG bytes. On a cache hit, if the entry is in Am it is promoted to the head of A1; if already in A1 it is moved to the head of A1. When admitting a completed sheet would exceed the 12 GiB bound, entries are evicted from the tail of Am first; only when Am is exhausted does eviction proceed from the tail of A1. The size split between Am and A1 is not fixed — both queues share the 12 GiB budget dynamically, with the only invariant that a promoted entry moves from Am to A1. This structure protects comparison sheets (repeatedly accessed) from being evicted by long sequential screening scans (one-use entries).
+
+All cache entries and replacement-policy metadata belong exclusively to this worker. Other nodes do not access files, pin previews, inspect policy counters, or depend on entries remaining warm.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q (two-queue FIFO with Am/A1 promotion) | LRU; Frequency-based eviction with aging | 2Q protects repeatedly accessed comparison sheets from being evicted by long sequential screening scans. The extra bookkeeping (two queues, promotion on hit) is accepted cost. LRU has lower overhead but is vulnerable to scan-driven eviction. Frequency-with-aging retains popular clips but adds counter maintenance and aging complexity, and can lag on project switches. All three policies keep the external interface, queue concurrency, and 12 GiB budget unchanged. |
