@@ -7,3 +7,8 @@
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a cache miss occurs and the new entry is admitted, the system SHALL insert it at the head of the Am queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a cache hit occurs on an entry in the Am queue, the system SHALL promote that entry to the head of the A1 queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a cache hit occurs on an entry in the A1 queue, the system SHALL move that entry to the head of the A1 queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When eviction is required to stay within the 12 GiB bound, the system SHALL evict entries from the tail of Am first, and only evict from the tail of A1 after Am is exhausted.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When an entry is promoted from Am to A1, the system SHALL transfer its size accounting from Am to A1 so the combined queue size never exceeds 12 GiB.
